{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sijie-Z/DocMind-RAG/pulls/490","id":4980461781,"node_id":"PR_kwDOSP5U4c8AAAABKNvQ1Q","html_url":"https://github.com/sijie-Z/DocMind-RAG/pull/490","diff_url":"https://github.com/sijie-Z/DocMind-RAG/pull/490.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/sijie-Z/DocMind-RAG/pull/490.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sijie-Z/DocMind-RAG/issues/490","number":490,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"feat(sdk): API Key 认证 + SSE 续传 + JSON-RPC（stdio/HTTP）与 Python/TS SDK (#480)","user":{"login":"sijie-Z","id":177101475,"node_id":"U_kgDOCo5aow","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177101475?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sijie-Z","html_url":"https://github.com/sijie-Z","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sijie-Z/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sijie-Z/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sijie-Z/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sijie-Z/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sijie-Z/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sijie-Z/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sijie-Z/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sijie-Z/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sijie-Z/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes #480\nEpic: #473\n\n## Summary\n- **API Key auth**: new `api_keys` table (bcrypt hash + 8-char prefix + JSON scopes + expiry/revocation/`last_used_at`); `dm_` keys coexist with JWT; management endpoints `POST/GET/DELETE /api/v1/api-keys`; `require_scope` wires `chat:write` into chat/agent write endpoints.\n- **SSE resume**: single `format_sse` encoder (`event`/`id`/`data`); per-stream Redis ring buffer (`INCR` / `LPUSH` / `LTRIM 0 999` / `EXPIRE`), `Last-Event-ID` replay, `SSE_RESUME_GONE`, disconnect keepalive up to `SSE_ORPHAN_TTL_SECONDS=600`; frontend parses `id`, forwards unknown events via `onEvent`, reconnects with `Last-Event-ID`.\n- **JSON-RPC 2.0**: transport-agnostic dispatcher (in-flight id table, concurrency, duplicate id `-32600`, out-of-order responses, bidirectional `session/request_permission`, 300s timeout treated as denial, `$/cancel_request`, disconnect cleanup); stdio NDJSON (1 MB line cap, stdout protocol-only) and `POST /api/v1/rpc` (web/agent bundle only, gated by `RPC_HTTP_ENABLED`, batch <= 20, API key + `rpc` scope).\n- **Methods**: `initialize`, `session/prompt` (Redis idempotency via `clientMessageId`, TTL 24h), `session/resume`, `session/wait`, `session/cancel`, `approvals/respond`, `tools/list`, `shutdown`; notifications `session.event` / `session.status`.\n- **SDKs**: Python (`Client` / `AsyncClient`; sessions / chat.stream / approvals / tools / knowledge; retries only for 429/502/503/504, never for streaming) and TypeScript (same surface, `AsyncIterable<SessionEvent>`, `AbortSignal`).\n- **Docs/ops**: ADR-007, facts synced (endpoint modules 28 / HTTP decorators 206 / tools 39 / SSE event types 24 / WS 3), OpenAPI path fix; migration `014_api_keys` (`down_revision=013_webhooks`).\n- **REST idempotency**: `payload.clientMessageId` on `/chat/stream` shares semantics with JSON-RPC `session/prompt` but uses a separate `rest:msg:*` key namespace.\n\n## Security hardening\n- SSE Redis keys are scoped by caller (`sse:buf:{scope}:{stream_id}`, scope `u{user_id}`), preventing cross-user replay and buffer injection; event ids remain `{stream_id}:{seq}`. Session ownership is also checked before replay. Documented in ADR-007.\n- `Last-Event-ID` requests are replay-only: they never re-run the pipeline (no duplicate answers, persistence, or LLM spend).\n- API keys are never logged; plaintext is returned once; invalid/expired/revoked keys fail with a uniform 401.\n\n## Accepted scope extensions\n- `core/prometheus.py` (RPC metrics), `models/__init__.py` (model registration), `docs/*` (facts anchors), SDK helper files, four existing SSE test parsers and the entrypoint module-count expectation: minimal mechanical adaptations.\n\n## Verification (real outputs)\n- `ruff check app/ tests/ scripts/ evals/` -> 0; `ruff format --check` -> 0.\n- `alembic upgrade head -> downgrade -1 -> upgrade head` (isolated DB) -> 0/0/0; `alembic heads` -> `014_api_keys (head)`; schema parity (migration vs `create_all`) -> 1 passed.\n- Dispatcher / SSE / API-key / SDK-file tests: 45 passed (API keys 8, SSE resume 7, SSE format 10, dispatcher 8, RPC HTTP 6, SDK key-file 6).\n- Post-sync regression: terminal 58 passed, webhook 94 passed, hooks 57 passed; outbound claims 10, entrypoints 10, i476 migration 1 passed.\n- stdio pipe: exactly 3 protocol frames (initialize protocolVersion=1 with 8 methods, tools/list 33 tools, shutdown ok); missing identity -> exit 2 with 0-byte stdout.\n- SDK: Python 9 passed; TypeScript `tsc --noEmit` clean and `npm test` 8 passed.\n- `--api-key-file` end-to-end: matching identity -> exit 0; mismatched `--user-id` -> exit 2, empty stdout, explicit stderr.\n- Mutation checks: disabling the API-key expiry window makes the expired-key test red; disabling `clientMessageId` idempotency makes the duplicate-prompt test red; both reverted and green.\n- Targeted acceptance suite: 39 passed; ruff/doc-facts green.\n\n## Rollback\n- Set `RPC_HTTP_ENABLED=false` to disable HTTP JSON-RPC (stdio unaffected).\n- Revoke all API keys (soft delete) or stop creating them; the JWT path is unchanged.\n- SSE `id` / `Last-Event-ID` are additive: legacy clients that ignore `id` keep working.\n\n## Known risks\n- Scoped Redis key switch: pre-existing unscoped buffers are unreachable for at most 1h (one-time release transient).\n- Resume/approval \"replay before claim\" has experiment-level but no committed regression test.\n- `--api-key-file` is optional; stdio identity still comes from CLI.\n- stdio line-limit boundary differs by 1 byte (newline included).\n- `session/wait` / `session/cancel` issued immediately after `session/prompt` may race background task creation (returns -32004).\n- API keys do not support in-place rotation (create -> switch -> revoke).\n","created_at":"2026-10-23T09:08:31Z","updated_at":"2026-10-23T09:08:31Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sijie-Z/DocMind-RAG/pulls/490/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sijie-Z/DocMind-RAG/pulls/490/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sijie-Z/DocMind-RAG/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sijie-Z/DocMind-RAG/issues/490/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sijie-Z/DocMind-RAG/statuses/43c420fc4b6342429ba9b5cd395bd3d394c2bbe3","head":{"label":"sijie-Z:feat/480-sdk","ref":"feat/480-sdk","sha":"43c420fc4b6342429ba9b5cd395bd3d394c2bbe3","user":{"login":"sijie-Z","id":177101475,"node_id":"U_kgDOCo5aow","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177101475?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sijie-Z","html_url":"https://github.com/sijie-Z","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sijie-Z/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sijie-Z/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sijie-Z/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sijie-Z/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sijie-Z/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sijie-Z/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sijie-Z/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sijie-Z/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sijie-Z/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"repo":{"id":1224627425,"node_id":"R_kgDOSP5U4Q","name":"D